  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Bai Ning Bing spins with an ice blade until sword traces become a tornado of ice.",
      "chapters": [
        134
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_bai_ning_bing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The cold flash-freezes blood; anyone caught in the blades is minced in seconds. Against Gu Yue clan fighters the storm can move several times faster than an earlier cast and hack a steel-shirted elder through many blows. When the storm ends, Bai Ning Bing’s held ice blade, already broken in two, still pierces that elder’s heart.",
      "chapters": [
        140
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_yue_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "She built the killer move from revolving Gu, whirlwind Gu, and Ice Blade Gu. By the Shang clan city battle stage she already judges that version fine for bullying rank two and substandard for rank three, and she is searching for a way to polish it.",
      "chapters": [
        299
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "early-pairing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_killer_moves",
        "gu_revolving_gu",
        "gu_whirlwind_gu",
        "gu_ice_blade_gu",
        "loc_shang_clan_city"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In ice crystal form, with vitality Gu keeping her organs alive, she stacks swirl Gu, Tornado Gu, Ice Edge Gu, Ice Crystal Gu, and continuous Frost Breath Gu until the killer move returns as ice blade storm. Five tasks at once stretch her mind to its limit; the tornado grows dense, drops the temperature, and can cut Yan Tu’s fiery snakes down to half size before they reform in flame. The revised storm still has a flaw: it lacks forward momentum and can only rotate on the spot when the frost-thick tornado will not advance, so she cannot kite while holding it. Yan Tu answers with fire sea twin dragon kill; after a long ice-and-fire stalemate she pretends to weaken, then inflates the storm to cripple his merged dragon, spends her aperture dry, and admits defeat.",
      "chapters": [
        314
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "revised-form-on-the-battle-stage",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
